   @merrimanr - Thought about this a bit more in context of @nickwallen's recent comments. Yeah, while the actual timeout setting itself can change, the _default_ should definitely not change on the fly. I can't think of a good reason why we would ever want a default to dynamically change. That's more of an upgrade/new release type of change imo that has documentation and release note implications.

