 Review comment:
   You raised a valid point which remind me a few more stuff to take into account in the constructor. I will add more comments.  

   However, I'm still not very much in favor of the static factory. It creates a very specialized rule that applies only for LogicalAggregates and uses a factory of Logical expressions which I am not sure if it corresponds to the most common use case. Moreover, helping the client use the constructor could also be part of the Javadoc. 

