 Review comment:
   This seems to have some unnecessary costs:
   - We're building up a List but we appear to know the exact length needed in advance.
   - We're building up one thing but then using LINQ to convert it to something else.

   Instead, why not do something like:
   ```C#
   var arrays = new IArrowArray[recordBachMessage.NodesLength];
   int bufferIndex = 0;
   for (int n = 0; n < recordBackMessage.NodesLength; n++)
   {
       int field = schema.GetFieldByIndex(n);
       var fieldNode = recordBatchMessage.Nodes(n).GetValueOrDefault();
       arrays[n] = field.DataType.IsFixedPrimitive() ?
           LoadPrimitiveField(field, fieldNode, recordBatchMessage, messageBuffer, ref bufferIndex) :
           LoadVariableField(field, fieldNode, recordBatchMessage, messageBuffer, ref bufferIndex);
   }
   return arrays;
   ```

