 Review comment:
   No, I don't think so. My understanding of Arrow is that there are really 2 formats:

   1. An Arrow "stream" - https://arrow.apache.org/docs/format/IPC.html#streaming-format
   2. An Arrow "file" - https://arrow.apache.org/docs/format/IPC.html#file-format

   You can see that the arrow file has a magic header and footer `ARROW1` and a `<FOOTER>` that contains the schema.  The Arrow "stream" format doesn't. So the user needs to tell the library which one they are dealing with. The way this works is the user either creates `new ArrowStreamReader` for (1) Arrow "stream" format and `new ArrowFileReader` for (2) Arrow file format.

