   It makes a copy. See https://github.com/apache/arrow/pull/3736/files#diff-59f21081ce1a3587c235beb879c0150fR147 below in this same class:


   ```c#
           protected override ArrowBuffer CreateArrowBuffer(ReadOnlyMemory<byte> data)
           {
               // need to use the Buffer.Builder because we are currently renting the memory to
               // read messages
               return new ArrowBuffer.Builder<byte>(data.Length)
                   .Append(data.Span)
                   .Build();
           }
   ```

   The extra copy will be addressed with [ARROW-4503: ArrowStreamReader allocates and copies data excessively](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ARROW-4503)


