 Review comment:
   Turns out I can't create a single `TimestampType` that can cater for all `TimeUnit` enum variants due to:

   ```rust
   fn get_data_type() -> DataType {
       $data_ty
   }
   ```

   This is because when implementing the above trait member, I can't know at runtime what `TimeUnit` the array is implementing.
   Is there a better/cleaner way of doing this?

