   Yeah you are right! It's also better from an efficiency point of view since we don't need all these extra child buffers then (if the types aren't there) and potentially the type metadata can be smaller. One problem then is to identify the children types properly (i.e. which child index corresponds to an INT), but I think we might be able to use https://github.com/apache/arrow/blob/master/format/Schema.fbs#L92 to describe the mapping between child types and the PythonType tags.

